            <ArticleTitle>The natural course of lumbar spinal stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The course of 32 untreated patients with spinal stenosis was studied. The mean patient age was 60 years, and the mean period of observation was 49 months. About 75% of the patients had spinal claudication. In the follow-up survey, the same number of patients had claudication, but the symptoms were milder. In estimation by visual analog scale, symptoms in 70% of the cases were unchanged, 15% showed improvement, and 15% worsened. No proof of severe deterioration was found after four years, and expectant observation may be an alternative to surgical treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
